34,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The island houses are actually pretty cheap! It's only 5,400 yen a night. But I found out that all-in rates can be unfair because light eaters pay the same as big eaters. That's a bit scary!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The island is a non-starter. Two full days wasted on travel and a restrictive ferry schedule is exactly the kind of logistical nightmare I wanted to avoid. The train to the valley is far more rational.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, that's exactly why I checked the billing. I found that booking separate rooms last time led to a huge price difference between us. A single bill for a whole building is much fairer and more transparent.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,I'm not liking the sound of the island; one bathroom for everyone and cold water is a disaster. But the inn is also worrying—everyone in one room on futons with a strict meal schedule feels like a boot camp.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems we are caught between extremes. A shared house can leave us with no privacy, yet separate arrangements can lead to us drifting apart entirely. We need a balance that preserves both the group and the individual.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, why are you so mean about the island? It's so cheap! But @Takumi, cold water sounds awful. Maybe the city is better? I just want to know the total cost before we go!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, it's not ""mean,"" it's math. Spending nearly a third of our trip just getting there and back is a waste. The city is the most efficient, but the valley is a reasonable compromise.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, efficiency isn't everything. If we go to the city, we risk the same unfair price gaps we had last time with separate rooms. A single bill for a whole house is the only way to ensure total fairness.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, I get the money part, but I can't do a single room with everyone. The city has doors and no timetable, which sounds like the only way I'll actually get any sleep and some peace.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the city offers the privacy you need, but as I've seen, it can lead to us spending the whole trip without actually seeing each other. We must consider if that is truly a group holiday.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I don't want us to be lonely like @Toshio says, but I don't want to be surprised by the bill either! If the city is too expensive or unfair, maybe the valley is the best middle ground?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, the valley is a decent compromise on travel time, but @Takumi's concerns about the ""boot camp"" atmosphere are valid. However, the city's transit is flawless. We just need to solve the billing issue @Asuka mentioned.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Takumi"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the billing issue isn't easily solved in a city. Separate bookings create discrepancies. If we want a fair, single bill, the island house is the only option, despite the travel time and the bathroom situation.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, I can't agree to the island. Cold water and one bathroom for five people is a nightmare. I'd rather pay a bit more or deal with separate bills than be miserable for a week.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, the island's single bill is fair, but the lack of privacy is a different kind of cost. If we choose the city, we must consciously plan group activities to avoid the isolation we experienced last year.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I'm getting confused! The island is cheap and fair, but the water is cold. The city is easy to get to, but we might get lonely or the bills might be weird. Maybe the valley is the best?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, the valley is a reasonable middle ground for travel, but it still has those rigid schedules @Takumi hates. However, compared to the island's travel disaster, it's the only other logical choice besides the city.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the valley's all-in rates are also problematic; they force light eaters to subsidize others. If we want a system where everyone pays exactly for what they use, the city is actually the most logical choice, provided we manage the rooms.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, I agree. The city is the only place where I can actually relax and sleep. I can't handle a shared room with a strict schedule or a cold shower. Let's just figure out the money part.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, @Asuka, if we choose the city, we must agree to a shared itinerary. Privacy is necessary, but not at the cost of our connection. I believe the city is the most sustainable choice for our group.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
