59,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I'm still a bit worried about the money, but I don't want anyone to be miserable! If the city means @Takumi can sleep and we aren't cold, I'm for it! I vote for the City Break!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,The city is the only option that doesn't waste our time or force us into a logistical bottleneck. It's the most rational choice for a group of adults and children. I vote for the City Break.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"While I still have concerns about the price discrepancies of separate rooms, the city is the only option that avoids the unfairness of all-in meal rates. For the sake of the group, I vote for the City Break.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,I'm definitely voting for the City Break. I can't deal with the island's bathroom or the inn's strict schedule. Having my own door and no timetable is the only way I'll actually enjoy the trip.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"The city provides the necessary space to prevent the friction of overcrowding, and as long as we commit to spending time together, it avoids the isolation of the past. I vote for the City Break.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
